WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.000
When you move in, check the meter on the first day and send the meter reading to your electricity and gas supplier: that way you only pay for your own use. Many bills are paid by direct debit. Check that the monthly amount matches what you use.

2
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Water is paid separately, to the water company for your area. TV Licence: you need one if you watch or record live TV on any channel, or if you use BBC iPlayer. It costs £180 a year.

3
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:46.900
Help: the Warm Home Discount (£150 off your electricity if you get certain benefits or have a low income), and many internet and mobile providers have cheaper «social tariffs» if you get Universal Credit.

4
00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:56.400
If you struggle to pay, talk to the company before you fall behind: they must offer you a payment plan.

5
00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:02.400
Say it aloud: “Can I set up a payment plan?”.
